Z||000002||87ECO5||01-01-2001||08:15 AM||||Got a response - here's Paul's note to me (I told him at least 30 people wanted them):<P>.<P><I>Hi Scott,<P>Your logo will be no problem, depending on a couple assumptions I've made and listed below.  If you can order 30 of them in one color I could do them all for $25.  If I have to make and ship them one at a time in different colors, then $5 each.  Shipping in the U.S. is included in the price, assuming a multiple order is shipped to one place.<P>My assumptions:<P>1. Material will be outdoor sign quality adhesive vinyl.<BR>2. Decals will be applied to the outside of the window.  (They can be applied to the inside, but you need to tell me because the image would have to be reversed so the adhesive is on the correct side.)<P>If you want to get the "clingy" type material that adheres to the inside of a window, that's possible also but will cost $50 for the setup fee and about $2 per decal, assuming an order of 25.  These would be printed on a clear square of material which would be applied to  the back window on the inside.<P>Hope this helps with your decision-making.<P>Regards,<P>Paul</I><P>.<P>I'll be focal point on this if you all want me to.  Let me know how (if) you want me to proceed ...||||reg||14
Z||000003||hugh||01-01-2001||10:18 AM||||If the style of decal can be agreed upon,I would want a few.I like both of what sqoach did.They don't have to be placed on just a Fiero.I still think a 3 inch diameter logo with a clear background and a border the same color as the logo about 1/4 to 3/8th inches in width is a good choice.Also,We cannot get a better person(as far as quality or honesty)than Paul.||||reg||1
